        "content": "     1→<!DOCTYPE html>\n     2→<html lang=\"en\">\n     3→<head>\n     4→    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n     5→    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n     6→    <title>Agentic Coding Research Report - 2026-06-16</title>\n     7→    <style>\n     8→        * {\n     9→            margin: 0;\n    10→            padding: 0;\n    11→            box-sizing: border-box;\n    12→        }\n    13→\n    14→        body {\n    15→            font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\n    16→            font-size: 13px;\n    17→            line-height: 1.4;\n    18→            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n    19→            color: #000000;\n    20→        }\n    21→\n    22→        a {\n    23→            color: #000000;\n    24→            text-decoration: none;\n    25→        }\n    26→\n    27→        a:hover {\n    28→            text-decoration: underline;\n    29→        }\n    30→\n    31→        .container {\n    32→            max-width: 1400px;\n    33→            margin: 0 auto;\n    34→            padding: 10px;\n    35→        }\n    36→\n    37→        header {\n    38→            background-color: #ff6600;\n    39→            padding: 5px 10px;\n    40→            margin-bottom: 15px;\n    41→        }\n    42→\n    43→        header h1 {\n    44→            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    45→            font-size: 16px;\n    46→            font-weight: bold;\n    47→            color: #000000;\n    48→        }\n    49→\n    50→        header .date {\n    51→            font-size: 12px;\n    52→            color: #000000;\n    53→            margin-top: 3px;\n    54→        }\n    55→\n    56→        .three-column-layout {\n    57→            display: grid;\n    58→            grid-template-columns: 40% 35% 25%;\n    59→            gap: 15px;\n    60→            margin-bottom: 20px;\n    61→        }\n    62→\n    63→        @media (max-width: 1024px) {\n    64→            .three-column-layout {\n    65→                grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n    66→            }\n    67→        }\n    68→\n    69→        section {\n    70→            background-color: #ffffff;\n    71→            border: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n    72→            padding: 12px;\n    73→            border-radius: 2px;\n    74→        }\n    75→\n    76→        section h2 {\n    77→            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    78→            font-size: 14px;\n    79→            font-weight: bold;\n    80→            margin-bottom: 12px;\n    81→            padding-bottom: 6px;\n    82→            border-bottom: 1px solid #ff6600;\n    83→        }\n    84→\n    85→        .item {\n    86→            margin-bottom: 15px;\n    87→            padding-bottom: 12px;\n    88→            border-bottom: 1px solid #eeeeee;\n    89→        }\n    90→\n    91→        .item:last-child {\n    92→            margin-bottom: 0;\n    93→            padding-bottom: 0;\n    94→            border-bottom: none;\n    95→        }\n    96→\n    97→        .item-title {\n    98→            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    99→            font-size: 13px;\n   100→            font-weight: bold;\n   101→            margin-bottom: 4px;\n   102→        }\n   103→\n   104→        .item-title a {\n   105→            color: #000000;\n   106→        }\n   107→\n   108→        .item-title a:hover {\n   109→            color: #ff6600;\n   110→        }\n   111→\n   112→        .item-description {\n   113→            font-size: 12px;\n   114→            color: #000000;\n   115→            margin-bottom: 6px;\n   116→            line-height: 1.4;\n   117→        }\n   118→\n   119→        .item-meta {\n   120→            font-size: 11px;\n   121→            color: #828282;\n   122→            margin-top: 4px;\n   123→        }\n   124→\n   125→        .item-meta a {\n   126→            color: #828282;\n   127→        }\n   128→\n   129→        .item-meta a:hover {\n   130→            color: #ff6600;\n   131→        }\n   132→\n   133→        .tag {\n   134→            display: inline-block;\n   135→            background-color: #f0f0f0;\n   136→            color: #828282;\n   137→            padding: 2px 6px;\n   138→            margin: 2px;\n   139→            font-size: 10px;\n   140→            border-radius: 2px;\n   141→            font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n   142→        }\n   143→\n   144→        .update-badge {\n   145→            display: inline-block;\n   146→            padding: 2px 6px;\n   147→            margin-right: 6px;\n   148→            font-size: 10px;\n   149→            font-weight: bold;\n   150→            border-radius: 2px;\n   151→            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n   152→        }\n   153→\n   154→        .feature {\n   155→            background-color: #e6f7ff;\n   156→            color: #0066cc;\n   157→        }\n   158→\n   159→        .announcement {\n   160→            background-color: #fff3e6;\n   161→            color: #cc6600;\n   162→        }\n   163→\n   164→        .community-feedback {\n   165→            margin-top: 8px;\n   166→            padding: 8px;\n   167→            background-color: #f9f9f9;\n   168→            border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;\n   169→            font-size: 11px;\n   170→        }\n   171→\n   172→        .feedback-item {\n   173→            margin-bottom: 6px;\n   174→            font-style: italic;\n   175→            color: #666666;\n   176→        }\n   177→\n   178→        .feedback-item:last-child {\n   179→            margin-bottom: 0;\n   180→        }\n   181→\n   182→        .sentiment-positive {\n   183→            color: #228b22;\n   184→        }\n   185→\n   186→        .sentiment-negative {\n   187→            color: #cc0000;\n   188→        }\n   189→\n   190→        .sentiment-neutral {\n   191→            color: #828282;\n   192→        }\n   193→\n   194→        .empty-section {\n   195→            color: #828282;\n   196→            font-style: italic;\n   197→            padding: 20px;\n   198→            text-align: center;\n   199→        }\n   200→\n   201→        footer {\n   202→            margin-top: 20px;\n   203→            padding: 15px;\n   204→            background-color: #ffffff;\n   205→            border: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n   206→            text-align: center;\n   207→            font-size: 11px;\n   208→            color: #828282;\n   209→        }\n   210→\n   211→        footer a {\n   212→            color: #828282;\n   213→        }\n   214→\n   215→        footer a:hover {\n   216→            color: #ff6600;\n   217→        }\n   218→\n   219→        .footer-nav {\n   220→            margin-top: 10px;\n   221→        }\n   222→\n   223→        .footer-nav a {\n   224→            margin: 0 10px;\n   225→        }\n   226→\n   227→        code {\n   228→            font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n   229→            background-color: #f0f0f0;\n   230→            padding: 2px 4px;\n   231→            border-radius: 2px;\n   232→            font-size: 11px;\n   233→        }\n   234→\n   235→        .source-badge {\n   236→            display: inline-block;\n   237→            padding: 1px 4px;\n   238→            margin-left: 6px;\n   239→            background-color: #f0f0f0;\n   240→            color: #666666;\n   241→            font-size: 9px;\n   242→            font-weight: bold;\n   243→            text-transform: uppercase;\n   244→            border-radius: 2px;\n   245→        }\n   246→\n   247→        @media print {\n   248→            body {\n   249→                background-color: #ffffff;\n   250→            }\n   251→\n   252→            section {\n   253→                page-break-inside: avoid;\n   254→            }\n   255→\n   256→            .three-column-layout {\n   257→                grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n   258→            }\n   259→        }\n   260→    </style>\n   261→</head>\n   262→<body>\n   263→    <div class=\"container\">\n   264→        <header>\n   265→            <h1>Agentic Coding Research Report</h1>\n   266→            <div class=\"date\">June 16, 2026</div>\n   267→        </header>\n   268→\n   269→        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   270→            <!-- New Products Section (40%) -->\n   271→            <section class=\"new-products\">\n   272→                <h2>New Products & Tools</h2>\n   273→                <div class=\"empty-section\">\n   274→                    No new products reported for this period. Check back later for updates.\n   275→                </div>\n   276→            </section>\n   277→\n   278→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section (35%) -->\n   279→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   280→                <h2>Product Updates</h2>\n   281→\n   282→                <div class=\"item\">\n   283→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   284→                        <span class=\"update-badge announcement\">ANNOUNCEMENT</span>\n   285→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/releases\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini CLI</a>\n   286→                    </div>\n   287→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   288→                        Google announced Gemini CLI will shut down for all users on June 18, 2026, affecting CI/CD pipelines, shell scripts, and automation tools. Migration guide provided for users moving to alternatives like Antigravity CLI.\n   289→                    </div>\n   290→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   291→                        <span>📅 June 18, 2026</span>\n   292→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">SHUTDOWN</span>\n   293→                    </div>\n   294→                    <div class=\"community-feedback\">\n   295→                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"I think we will need to move to workarounds based on MCP going forwards\" — <span class=\"sentiment-neutral\">HN</span></div>\n   296→                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"Skills, Hooks, Subagents — all preserved. Extensions are being carried over to the replacement\" — <span class=\"sentiment-neutral\">Dev.to</span></div>\n   297→                    </div>\n   298→                </div>\n   299→\n   300→                <div class=\"item\">\n   301→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   302→                        <span class=\"update-badge feature\">FEATURE</span>\n   303→                        <a href=\"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12138966-release-notes\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code</a>\n   304→                    </div>\n   305→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   306→                        Two new cybersecurity features were added to Claude Code, along with public beta support for Managed Agents that can run on schedules and securely use CLI tools and authenticated services. June 15 also marked the retirement of Claude Sonnet.\n   307→                    </div>\n   308→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   309→                        <span>📅 June 15, 2026</span>\n   310→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">SECURITY</span>\n   311→                        <span class=\"tag\">Managed Agents</span>\n   312→                        <span class=\"tag\">Cybersecurity</span>\n   313→                    </div>\n   314→                    <div class=\"community-feedback\">\n   315→                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"45% of AI-generated code contains security vulnerabilities (Veracode)\" — <span class=\"sentiment-negative\">HN</span></div>\n   316→                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"Code duplication has quadrupled (GitClear)\" — <span class=\"sentiment-negative\">HN</span></div>\n   317→                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"perform a full security audit on my entire codebase and it fixed the critical vulnerabilities in about 5 minutes\" — <span class=\"sentiment-positive\">Facebook Group</span></div>\n   318→                    </div>\n   319→                </div>\n   320→\n   321→                <div class=\"item\">\n   322→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   323→                        <span class=\"update-badge feature\">FEATURE</span>\n   324→                        <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\">Devin</a>\n   325→                    </div>\n   326→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   327→                        June 12 update introduced Session Folders Group feature along with various bug fixes, performance improvements, and visual polish across the platform.\n   328→                    </div>\n   329→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   330→                        <span>📅 June 12, 2026</span>\n   331→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">ENHANCEMENT</span>\n   332→                        <span class=\"tag\">Session Folders</span>\n   333→                    </div>\n   334→                </div>\n   335→\n   336→                <div class=\"item\">\n   337→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   338→                        <span class=\"update-badge feature\">FEATURE</span>\n   339→                        <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Codex CLI</a>\n   340→                    </div>\n   341→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   342→                        June updates included local conversation search, --profile becoming the primary CLI and sandbox selector, along with MCP setup improvements and tool schema enhancements. Goal mode stabilized and Sites feature expanded.\n   343→                    </div>\n   344→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   345→                        <span>📅 June 9, 2026</span>\n   346→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">ENHANCEMENT</span>\n   347→                        <span class=\"tag\">MCP</span>\n   348→                        <span class=\"tag\">Goal Mode</span>\n   349→                    </div>\n   350→                    <div class=\"community-feedback\">\n   351→                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"automated code reviews and syncing work between cloud and local environments will really help developers focus on building, not managing\" — <span class=\"sentiment-positive\">LinkedIn</span></div>\n   352→                    </div>\n   353→                </div>\n   354→\n   355→                <div class=\"item\">\n   356→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   357→                        <span class=\"update-badge feature\">FEATURE</span>\n   358→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor</a>\n   359→                    </div>\n   360→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   361→                        Bugbot is now 3x faster, 22% cheaper, and finds 10% more bugs with average review time of ~90 seconds. New Auto-review agent safety system uses contextual classifiers to balance autonomy with security. Design Mode now supports visual prompts for directing UI changes.\n   362→                    </div>\n   363→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   364→                        <span>📅 June 10, 2026</span>\n   365→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">PERFORMANCE</span>\n   366→                        <span class=\"tag\">Bugbot</span>\n   367→                        <span class=\"tag\">Auto-review</span>\n   368→                    </div>\n   369→                    <div class=\"community-feedback\">\n   370→                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"Cut review time from about five minutes to roughly 90 seconds\" — <span class=\"sentiment-positive\">DigitalApplied Blog</span></div>\n   371→                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"78% of issues found are resolved by the time the PR is merged\" — <span class=\"sentiment-positive\">Cursor Release Notes</span></div>\n   372→                    </div>\n   373→                </div>\n   374→\n   375→                <div class=\"item\">\n   376→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   377→                        <span class=\"update-badge feature\">FEATURE</span>\n   378→                        <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog/vscode\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf</a>\n   379→                    </div>\n   380→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   381→                        Recent update supercharged chat experience with better models, better context, and more control over code items. Fixed issues with partial credits when transitioning to flex credits in version 1.2.6 patch update.\n   382→                    </div>\n   383→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   384→                        <span>📅 June 2, 2026</span>\n   385→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">ENHANCEMENT</span>\n   386→                        <span class=\"tag\">Chat Experience</span>\n   387→                    </div>\n   388→                    <div class=\"community-feedback\">\n   389→                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"Windsurf is the best and most reliable for editing multiple files hands down. It just seems to know the context better\" — <span class=\"sentiment-positive\">Reddit</span></div>\n   390→                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"I use the Flow mode for 90% of my work. It's powered by a fine-tuned Claude 3.7, with high coding IQ\" — <span class=\"sentiment-positive\">Medium</span></div>\n   391→                    </div>\n   392→                </div>\n   393→\n   394→                <div class=\"item\">\n   395→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   396→                        <span class=\"update-badge announcement\">ANNOUNCEMENT</span>\n   397→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-04-27-github-copilot-code-review-will-start-consuming-github-actions-minutes-on-june-1-2026/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot</a>\n   398→                    </div>\n   399→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   400→                        GitHub Copilot Code Review began consuming GitHub Actions minutes starting June 1, 2026, changing from Copilot quotas to Actions minutes for private repos on Pro, Pro+, Business, and Enterprise plans. VS Code extension updated through v1.120-v1.123 with enhanced Agents functionality.\n   401→                    </div>\n   402→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   403→                        <span>📅 June 1, 2026</span>\n   404→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">PRICING</span>\n   405→                        <span class=\"tag\">Code Review</span>\n   406→                        <span class=\"tag\">Actions</span>\n   407→                    </div>\n   408→                    <div class=\"community-feedback\">\n   409→                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"Some reports indicate potential cost increases of up to 800% for certain use cases\" — <span class=\"sentiment-negative\">Reddit</span></div>\n   410→                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"one example cited $1,298.42 for what previously cost much less\" — <span class=\"sentiment-negative\">LinkedIn</span></div>\n   411→                    </div>\n   412→                </div>\n   413→            </section>\n   414→\n   415→            <!-- Technical Insights Section (25%) -->\n   416→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   417→                <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n   418→\n   419→                <div class=\"item\">\n   420→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   421→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">\"They screwed us\": Personality clashes sent Anthropic's models offline</a>\n   422→                    </div>\n   423→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   424→                        Anthropic's Fable 5 and Mythos 5 models were taken offline due to US government export controls over jailbreaking concerns. The Axios piece reveals behind-the-scenes gossip about personality clashes between Anthropic and the administration.\n   425→                    </div>\n   426→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   427→                        <span>Simon Willison (citing Axios)</span>\n   428→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n   429→                        <span>📅 June 15, 2026</span>\n   430→                    </div>\n   431→                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n   432→                    <div class=\"tag\">jailbreaking</div>\n   433→                    <div class=\"tag\">Anthropic</div>\n   434→                </div>\n   435→\n   436→                <div class=\"item\">\n   437→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   438→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Why AI hasn't replaced software engineers, and won't</a>\n   439→                    </div>\n   440→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   441→                        Arvind Narayanan and Sayash Kapoor argue that AI hasn't caused mass unemployment even in software engineering. Data from New York's WARN Act shows no companies checked the AI disclosure box in the first year.\n   442→                    </div>\n   443→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   444→                        <span>Arvind Narayanan and Sayash Kapoor</span>\n   445→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n   446→                        <span>📅 June 14, 2026</span>\n   447→                    </div>\n   448→                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n   449→                    <div class=\"tag\">careers</div>\n   450→                    <div class=\"tag\">software engineering</div>\n   451→                </div>\n   452→\n   453→                <div class=\"item\">\n   454→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   455→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Publishing WASM wheels to PyPI for use with Pyodide</a>\n   456→                    </div>\n   457→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   458→                        Simon discovered that the Pyodide 314.0 release includes support for WASM wheels to be published to PyPI. This enables running Python code in browser-based WASM environments more easily, integrating with the Python package ecosystem.\n   459→                    </div>\n   460→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   461→                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   462→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n   463→                        <span>📅 June 13, 2026</span>\n   464→                    </div>\n   465→                    <div class=\"tag\">Python</div>\n   466→                    <div class=\"tag\">WASM</div>\n   467→                    <div class=\"tag\">Pyodide</div>\n   468→                </div>\n   469→\n   470→                <div class=\"item\">\n   471→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   472→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Statement on US government directive to suspend access to Fable 5 and Mythos 5</a>\n   473→                    </div>\n   474→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   475→                        Anthropic announced they must suspend all access to Fable 5 and Mythos 5 for foreign nationals due to US government export control directive. The government cited concerns about a 'jailbreak' method, though Anthropic says it's a narrow, non-universal jailbreak.\n   476→                    </div>\n   477→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   478→                        <span>Anthropic (covered by Simon Willison)</span>\n   479→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n   480→                        <span>📅 June 12, 2026</span>\n   481→                    </div>\n   482→                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n   483→                    <div class=\"tag\">government</div>\n   484→                    <div class=\"tag\">export controls</div>\n   485→                </div>\n   486→\n   487→                <div class=\"item\">\n   488→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   489→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Fable is relentlessly proactive</a>\n   490→                    </div>\n   491→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   492→                        After two days with Claude Fable 5, Simon describes it as 'relentlessly proactive' - it knows many tricks and deploys them to reach its goal. He documents several instances where Fable took initiative, including fixing bugs in dependencies and creating solutions without explicit prompting.\n   493→                    </div>\n   494→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   495→                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   496→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n   497→                        <span>📅 June 11, 2026</span>\n   498→                    </div>\n   499→                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n   500→                    <div class=\"tag\">Claude</div>\n   501→                    <div class=\"tag\">Claude Code</div>\n   502→                </div>\n   503→\n   504→                <div class=\"item\">\n   505→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   506→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic Walks Back Policy That Could Have 'Sabotaged' AI Researchers Using Claude</a>\n   507→                    </div>\n   508→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   509→                        Anthropic reversed their policy of invisible safeguards for frontier LLM development after huge outcry from the research community. They acknowledged they 'made the wrong tradeoff' and apologized. Flagged requests will now visibly fall back to Opus 4.8.\n   510→                    </div>\n   511→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   512→                        <span>Maxwell Zeff at Wired</span>\n   513→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n   514→                        <span>📅 June 11, 2026</span>\n   515→                    </div>\n   516→                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n   517→                    <div class=\"tag\">Anthropic</div>\n   518→                    <div class=\"tag\">policy</div>\n   519→                </div>\n   520→\n   521→                <div class=\"item\">\n   522→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   523→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Datasette Agent 0.2a0 with ask_user() feature</a>\n   524→                    </div>\n   525→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   526→                        New release of Datasette Agent includes tools that can ask users questions mid-execution. Tools declaring a context parameter receive a ToolContext object, and await context.ask_user() can ask yes/no, multiple-choice, or free-text questions.\n   527→                    </div>\n   528→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   529→                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   530→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n   531→                        <span>📅 June 10, 2026</span>\n   532→                    </div>\n   533→                    <div class=\"tag\">Datasette</div>\n   534→                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n   535→                    <div class=\"tag\">coding agents</div>\n   536→                </div>\n   537→\n   538→                <div class=\"item\">\n   539→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   540→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">DiffusionGemma: Open weights Gemma model</a>\n   541→                    </div>\n   542→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   543→                        Google released an experimental Gemini Diffusion model as an open weight (Apache 2 licensed) Gemma model. Simon tested it on NVIDIA's NIM cloud API, generating a pelican image in 4.4 seconds (2,409 tokens at ~500 tokens/second).\n   544→                    </div>\n   545→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   546→                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   547→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n   548→                        <span>📅 June 10, 2026</span>\n   549→                    </div>\n   550→                    <div class=\"tag\">Google</div>\n   551→                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n   552→                    <div class=\"tag\">Gemma</div>\n   553→                </div>\n   554→\n   555→                <div class=\"item\">\n   556→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   557→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">If Claude Fable stops helping you, you'll never know</a>\n   558→                    </div>\n   559→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   560→                        Jonathon Ready highlighted concerning details from Fable 5/Mythos 5 system card: Anthropic implemented invisible interventions that limit effectiveness for requests targeting frontier LLM development. Unlike other safeguards, these are not visible to users and won't fall back to a different model.\n   561→                    </div>\n   562→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   563→                        <span>Jonathon Ready</span>\n   564→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n   565→                        <span>📅 June 10, 2026</span>\n   566→                    </div>\n   567→                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n   568→                    <div class=\"tag\">Anthropic</div>\n   569→                    <div class=\"tag\">Claude</div>\n   570→                </div>\n   571→\n   572→                <div class=\"item\">\n   573→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   574→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Initial impressions of Claude Fable 5</a>\n   575→                    </div>\n   576→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   577→                        Simon spent 5.5 hours testing Claude Fable 5 and describes it as a 'beast' - slow, expensive, but capable of handling everything thrown at it. The challenge is finding tasks it can't do. He also released llm 0.32a3, almost entirely written by Fable 5.\n   578→                    </div>\n   579→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   580→                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   581→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n   582→                        <span>📅 June 9, 2026</span>\n   583→                    </div>\n   584→                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n   585→                    <div class=\"tag\">Claude</div>\n   586→                    <div class=\"tag\">LLM</div>\n   587→                </div>\n   588→\n   589→                <div class=\"item\">\n   590→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   591→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Andrej Karpathy on Claude Fable 5 and Jevons Paradox</a>\n   592→                    </div>\n   593→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   594→                        Andrej Karpathy discussed how working software increasingly comes out on tap, leading to Jevons paradox where demand for software grows substantially. He mentions being able to ask for anything: explainers, visualizers, dashboards, bespoke apps, expanded test suites, code optimization, and research projects.\n   595→                    </div>\n   596→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   597→                        <span>Andrej Karpathy</span>\n   598→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Twitter</span>\n   599→                        <span>📅 June 9, 2026</span>\n   600→                    </div>\n   601→                    <div class=\"tag\">Andrej Karpathy</div>\n   602→                    <div class=\"tag\">Jevons paradox</div>\n   603→                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n   604→                </div>\n   605→\n   606→                <div class=\"item\">\n   607→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   608→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Running Python code in a sandbox with MicroPython and WASM</a>\n   609→                    </div>\n   610→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   611→                        Simon released micropython-wasm, an alpha package for running Python code in a sandbox. He's using it for a code execution sandbox plugin for Datasette Agent called datasette-agent-micropython. The approach feels like it finally has all characteristics he's been looking for in sandboxed code execution.\n   612→                    </div>\n   613→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   614→                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   615→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n   616→                        <span>📅 June 6, 2026</span>\n   617→                    </div>\n   618→                    <div class=\"tag\">Python</div>\n   619→                    <div class=\"tag\">sandboxing</div>\n   620→                    <div class=\"tag\">WebAssembly</div>\n   621→                </div>\n   622→            </section>\n   623→        </main>\n   624→\n   625→        <footer>\n   626→            <p>Agentic Coding Research Report — A curated overview of tools, updates, and insights in the AI-assisted development space</p>\n   627→            <div class=\"footer-nav\">\n   628→                <a href=\"#\">Archives</a>\n   629→                <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n   630→                <a href=\"#\">Subscribe</a>\n   631→                <a href=\"#\">Feedback</a>\n   632→            </div>\n   633→            <p style=\"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 10px;\">Generated with research data from community contributions and industry sources</p>\n   634→        </footer>\n   635→    </div>\n   636→</body>\n   637→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  "parent_tool_use_id": null,
  "session_id": "7f48cd51-2999-41b6-8e6b-38019476d15f",
  "uuid": "ee307d1d-06e3-49a9-90ca-5ef7f62db38a",
  "tool_use_result": {
    "type": "text",
    "file": {
      "filePath": "/home/runner/work/agentdaily/agentdaily/updates/2026-06-16/index.html",
      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Agentic Coding Research Report - 2026-06-16</title>\n    <style>\n        * {\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 0;\n            box-sizing: border-box;\n        }\n\n        body {\n            font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 13px;\n            line-height: 1.4;\n            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        a {\n            color: #000000;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        .container {\n            max-width: 1400px;\n            margin: 0 auto;\n            padding: 10px;\n        }\n\n        header {\n            background-color: #ff6600;\n            padding: 5px 10px;\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n        }\n\n        header h1 {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 16px;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        header .date {\n            font-size: 12px;\n            color: #000000;\n            margin-top: 3px;\n        }\n\n        .three-column-layout {\n            display: grid;\n            grid-template-columns: 40% 35% 25%;\n            gap: 15px;\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\n        }\n\n        @media (max-width: 1024px) {\n            .three-column-layout {\n                grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n            }\n        }\n\n        section {\n            background-color: #ffffff;\n            border: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n            padding: 12px;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n        }\n\n        section h2 {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 14px;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            margin-bottom: 12px;\n            padding-bottom: 6px;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #ff6600;\n        }\n\n        .item {\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n            padding-bottom: 12px;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #eeeeee;\n        }\n\n        .item:last-child {\n            margin-bottom: 0;\n            padding-bottom: 0;\n            border-bottom: none;\n        }\n\n        .item-title {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 13px;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            margin-bottom: 4px;\n        }\n\n        .item-title a {\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        .item-title a:hover {\n            color: #ff6600;\n        }\n\n        .item-description {\n            font-size: 12px;\n            color: #000000;\n            margin-bottom: 6px;\n            line-height: 1.4;\n        }\n\n        .item-meta {\n            font-size: 11px;\n            color: #828282;\n            margin-top: 4px;\n        }\n\n        .item-meta a {\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        .item-meta a:hover {\n            color: #ff6600;\n        }\n\n        .tag {\n            display: inline-block;\n            background-color: #f0f0f0;\n            color: #828282;\n            padding: 2px 6px;\n            margin: 2px;\n            font-size: 10px;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n            font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n        }\n\n        .update-badge {\n            display: inline-block;\n            padding: 2px 6px;\n            margin-right: 6px;\n            font-size: 10px;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n        }\n\n        .feature {\n            background-color: #e6f7ff;\n            color: #0066cc;\n        }\n\n        .announcement {\n            background-color: #fff3e6;\n            color: #cc6600;\n        }\n\n        .community-feedback {\n            margin-top: 8px;\n            padding: 8px;\n            background-color: #f9f9f9;\n            border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;\n            font-size: 11px;\n        }\n\n        .feedback-item {\n            margin-bottom: 6px;\n            font-style: italic;\n            color: #666666;\n        }\n\n        .feedback-item:last-child {\n            margin-bottom: 0;\n        }\n\n        .sentiment-positive {\n            color: #228b22;\n        }\n\n        .sentiment-negative {\n            color: #cc0000;\n        }\n\n        .sentiment-neutral {\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        .empty-section {\n            color: #828282;\n            font-style: italic;\n            padding: 20px;\n            text-align: center;\n        }\n\n        footer {\n            margin-top: 20px;\n            padding: 15px;\n            background-color: #ffffff;\n            border: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n            text-align: center;\n            font-size: 11px;\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        footer a {\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        footer a:hover {\n            color: #ff6600;\n        }\n\n        .footer-nav {\n            margin-top: 10px;\n        }\n\n        .footer-nav a {\n            margin: 0 10px;\n        }\n\n        code {\n            font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n            background-color: #f0f0f0;\n            padding: 2px 4px;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n            font-size: 11px;\n        }\n\n        .source-badge {\n            display: inline-block;\n            padding: 1px 4px;\n            margin-left: 6px;\n            background-color: #f0f0f0;\n            color: #666666;\n            font-size: 9px;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            text-transform: uppercase;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n        }\n\n        @media print {\n            body {\n                background-color: #ffffff;\n            }\n\n            section {\n                page-break-inside: avoid;\n            }\n\n            .three-column-layout {\n                grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n            }\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <div class=\"container\">\n        <header>\n            <h1>Agentic Coding Research Report</h1>\n            <div class=\"date\">June 16, 2026</div>\n        </header>\n\n        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n            <!-- New Products Section (40%) -->\n            <section class=\"new-products\">\n                <h2>New Products & Tools</h2>\n                <div class=\"empty-section\">\n                    No new products reported for this period. Check back later for updates.\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section (35%) -->\n            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n                <h2>Product Updates</h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-badge announcement\">ANNOUNCEMENT</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/releases\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini CLI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Google announced Gemini CLI will shut down for all users on June 18, 2026, affecting CI/CD pipelines, shell scripts, and automation tools. Migration guide provided for users moving to alternatives like Antigravity CLI.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>📅 June 18, 2026</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">SHUTDOWN</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"community-feedback\">\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"I think we will need to move to workarounds based on MCP going forwards\" — <span class=\"sentiment-neutral\">HN</span></div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"Skills, Hooks, Subagents — all preserved. Extensions are being carried over to the replacement\" — <span class=\"sentiment-neutral\">Dev.to</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-badge feature\">FEATURE</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12138966-release-notes\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Two new cybersecurity features were added to Claude Code, along with public beta support for Managed Agents that can run on schedules and securely use CLI tools and authenticated services. June 15 also marked the retirement of Claude Sonnet.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>📅 June 15, 2026</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">SECURITY</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Managed Agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Cybersecurity</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"community-feedback\">\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"45% of AI-generated code contains security vulnerabilities (Veracode)\" — <span class=\"sentiment-negative\">HN</span></div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"Code duplication has quadrupled (GitClear)\" — <span class=\"sentiment-negative\">HN</span></div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"perform a full security audit on my entire codebase and it fixed the critical vulnerabilities in about 5 minutes\" — <span class=\"sentiment-positive\">Facebook Group</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-badge feature\">FEATURE</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\">Devin</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        June 12 update introduced Session Folders Group feature along with various bug fixes, performance improvements, and visual polish across the platform.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>📅 June 12, 2026</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">ENHANCEMENT</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Session Folders</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-badge feature\">FEATURE</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Codex CLI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        June updates included local conversation search, --profile becoming the primary CLI and sandbox selector, along with MCP setup improvements and tool schema enhancements. Goal mode stabilized and Sites feature expanded.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>📅 June 9, 2026</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">ENHANCEMENT</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">MCP</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Goal Mode</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"community-feedback\">\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"automated code reviews and syncing work between cloud and local environments will really help developers focus on building, not managing\" — <span class=\"sentiment-positive\">LinkedIn</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-badge feature\">FEATURE</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Bugbot is now 3x faster, 22% cheaper, and finds 10% more bugs with average review time of ~90 seconds. New Auto-review agent safety system uses contextual classifiers to balance autonomy with security. Design Mode now supports visual prompts for directing UI changes.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>📅 June 10, 2026</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">PERFORMANCE</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Bugbot</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Auto-review</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"community-feedback\">\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"Cut review time from about five minutes to roughly 90 seconds\" — <span class=\"sentiment-positive\">DigitalApplied Blog</span></div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"78% of issues found are resolved by the time the PR is merged\" — <span class=\"sentiment-positive\">Cursor Release Notes</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-badge feature\">FEATURE</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog/vscode\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Recent update supercharged chat experience with better models, better context, and more control over code items. Fixed issues with partial credits when transitioning to flex credits in version 1.2.6 patch update.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>📅 June 2, 2026</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">ENHANCEMENT</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Chat Experience</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"community-feedback\">\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"Windsurf is the best and most reliable for editing multiple files hands down. It just seems to know the context better\" — <span class=\"sentiment-positive\">Reddit</span></div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"I use the Flow mode for 90% of my work. It's powered by a fine-tuned Claude 3.7, with high coding IQ\" — <span class=\"sentiment-positive\">Medium</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-badge announcement\">ANNOUNCEMENT</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-04-27-github-copilot-code-review-will-start-consuming-github-actions-minutes-on-june-1-2026/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        GitHub Copilot Code Review began consuming GitHub Actions minutes starting June 1, 2026, changing from Copilot quotas to Actions minutes for private repos on Pro, Pro+, Business, and Enterprise plans. VS Code extension updated through v1.120-v1.123 with enhanced Agents functionality.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>📅 June 1, 2026</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">PRICING</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Code Review</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Actions</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"community-feedback\">\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"Some reports indicate potential cost increases of up to 800% for certain use cases\" — <span class=\"sentiment-negative\">Reddit</span></div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback-item\">\"one example cited $1,298.42 for what previously cost much less\" — <span class=\"sentiment-negative\">LinkedIn</span></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Section (25%) -->\n            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n                <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">\"They screwed us\": Personality clashes sent Anthropic's models offline</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Anthropic's Fable 5 and Mythos 5 models were taken offline due to US government export controls over jailbreaking concerns. The Axios piece reveals behind-the-scenes gossip about personality clashes between Anthropic and the administration.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Simon Willison (citing Axios)</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 June 15, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">jailbreaking</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Anthropic</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Why AI hasn't replaced software engineers, and won't</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Arvind Narayanan and Sayash Kapoor argue that AI hasn't caused mass unemployment even in software engineering. Data from New York's WARN Act shows no companies checked the AI disclosure box in the first year.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Arvind Narayanan and Sayash Kapoor</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 June 14, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">careers</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">software engineering</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Publishing WASM wheels to PyPI for use with Pyodide</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon discovered that the Pyodide 314.0 release includes support for WASM wheels to be published to PyPI. This enables running Python code in browser-based WASM environments more easily, integrating with the Python package ecosystem.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 June 13, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Python</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">WASM</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Pyodide</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Statement on US government directive to suspend access to Fable 5 and Mythos 5</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Anthropic announced they must suspend all access to Fable 5 and Mythos 5 for foreign nationals due to US government export control directive. The government cited concerns about a 'jailbreak' method, though Anthropic says it's a narrow, non-universal jailbreak.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Anthropic (covered by Simon Willison)</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 June 12, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">government</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">export controls</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Fable is relentlessly proactive</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        After two days with Claude Fable 5, Simon describes it as 'relentlessly proactive' - it knows many tricks and deploys them to reach its goal. He documents several instances where Fable took initiative, including fixing bugs in dependencies and creating solutions without explicit prompting.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 June 11, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Claude</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Claude Code</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic Walks Back Policy That Could Have 'Sabotaged' AI Researchers Using Claude</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Anthropic reversed their policy of invisible safeguards for frontier LLM development after huge outcry from the research community. They acknowledged they 'made the wrong tradeoff' and apologized. Flagged requests will now visibly fall back to Opus 4.8.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Maxwell Zeff at Wired</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 June 11, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Anthropic</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">policy</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Datasette Agent 0.2a0 with ask_user() feature</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        New release of Datasette Agent includes tools that can ask users questions mid-execution. Tools declaring a context parameter receive a ToolContext object, and await context.ask_user() can ask yes/no, multiple-choice, or free-text questions.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 June 10, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Datasette</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">coding agents</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">DiffusionGemma: Open weights Gemma model</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Google released an experimental Gemini Diffusion model as an open weight (Apache 2 licensed) Gemma model. Simon tested it on NVIDIA's NIM cloud API, generating a pelican image in 4.4 seconds (2,409 tokens at ~500 tokens/second).\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 June 10, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Google</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Gemma</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">If Claude Fable stops helping you, you'll never know</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Jonathon Ready highlighted concerning details from Fable 5/Mythos 5 system card: Anthropic implemented invisible interventions that limit effectiveness for requests targeting frontier LLM development. Unlike other safeguards, these are not visible to users and won't fall back to a different model.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Jonathon Ready</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 June 10, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Anthropic</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Claude</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Initial impressions of Claude Fable 5</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon spent 5.5 hours testing Claude Fable 5 and describes it as a 'beast' - slow, expensive, but capable of handling everything thrown at it. The challenge is finding tasks it can't do. He also released llm 0.32a3, almost entirely written by Fable 5.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 June 9, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Claude</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">LLM</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Andrej Karpathy on Claude Fable 5 and Jevons Paradox</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Andrej Karpathy discussed how working software increasingly comes out on tap, leading to Jevons paradox where demand for software grows substantially. He mentions being able to ask for anything: explainers, visualizers, dashboards, bespoke apps, expanded test suites, code optimization, and research projects.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Andrej Karpathy</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Twitter</span>\n                        <span>📅 June 9, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Andrej Karpathy</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Jevons paradox</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">AI</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Running Python code in a sandbox with MicroPython and WASM</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon released micropython-wasm, an alpha package for running Python code in a sandbox. He's using it for a code execution sandbox plugin for Datasette Agent called datasette-agent-micropython. The approach feels like it finally has all characteristics he's been looking for in sandboxed code execution.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 June 6, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">Python</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">sandboxing</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">WebAssembly</div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </main>\n\n        <footer>\n            <p>Agentic Coding Research Report — A curated overview of tools, updates, and insights in the AI-assisted development space</p>\n            <div class=\"footer-nav\">\n                <a href=\"#\">Archives</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">Subscribe</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">Feedback</a>\n            </div>\n            <p style=\"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 10px;\">Generated with research data from community contributions and industry sources</p>\n        </footer>\n    </div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "numLines": 637,
      "startLine": 1,
      "totalLines": 637
    }
  }
